From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:51:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] edid: take the extension count of an HDMI Forum EEODB

HDMI 2.1 (10.3.6) lets a sink count its extension blocks in an HDMI
Forum EDID Extension Override Data Block (HF-EEODB), the first data
block of block 1, a CTA-861 extension of revision 3 or later, in place
of the count of the base block: a sink with more than 255 of them, or
one whose base block counts fewer for older sources. A Samsung Odyssey
G60SD on HDMI gives 384 bytes, a base block that counts 1 extension and
an HF-EEODB that counts 2; _di_edid_parse() took the count of the base
block alone, said "The data size does not match the encoded block
count." and left its third block, a DisplayID 2 extension, unread.

parse_hf_eeodb_ext_count() reads the count of an HF-EEODB as the kernel
does (drm_edid.c, edid_hfeeodb_extension_block_count()): only where the
base block counts at least one extension, block 1 is a CTA-861
extension of revision 3 or later whose data block collection has room
for it, and its first data block is an extended one of tag 0x78 with a
payload of at least 2 bytes. That count then stands for the one of the
base block; the checks against the size of the data are as before.
---
 edid.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/edid.c b/edid.c
index c6d21a8..f46458e 100644
--- a/edid.c
+++ b/edid.c
@@ -69,6 +69,34 @@ parse_ext_count(const uint8_t data[static EDID_BLOCK_SIZE])
 	return data[0x7E];
 }
 
+/**
+ * The extension block count of an HDMI Forum EDID Extension Override Data
+ * Block (HF-EEODB, HDMI 2.1 10.3.6), or 0 where there is none. A sink that
+ * has more than 255 extension blocks, or one whose base block counts fewer
+ * blocks than it has for an older source, puts it first in the data block
+ * collection of block 1, a CTA-861 extension of revision 3 or later; its
+ * count then replaces the one of the base block. The same rule as the
+ * kernel's (drm_edid.c, edid_hfeeodb_extension_block_count()).
+ */
+static size_t
+parse_hf_eeodb_ext_count(const uint8_t *data, size_t size)
+{
+	const uint8_t *cta;
+
+	if (size < 2 * EDID_BLOCK_SIZE || parse_ext_count(data) == 0)
+		return 0;
+	cta = &data[EDID_BLOCK_SIZE];
+	/* a CTA-861 extension of revision 3 or later, with a data block
+	 * collection of at least the three bytes of the HF-EEODB */
+	if (cta[0] != 0x02 || cta[1] < 3 || cta[2] < 4 + 3)
+		return 0;
+	/* extended tag (7), a payload of at least 2 bytes, extended tag code
+	 * 0x78 */
+	if ((cta[4] >> 5) != 7 || (cta[4] & 0x1F) < 2 || cta[5] != 0x78)
+		return 0;
+	return cta[6];
+}
+
 static bool
 validate_block_checksum(const uint8_t data[static EDID_BLOCK_SIZE])
 {
@@ -1283,6 +1311,8 @@ _di_edid_parse(const void *data, size_t size, FILE *failure_msg_file)
 
 	exts_len = (size / EDID_BLOCK_SIZE) - 1;
 	parsed_ext_len = parse_ext_count(data);
+	if (parse_hf_eeodb_ext_count(data, size) > 0)
+		parsed_ext_len = parse_hf_eeodb_ext_count(data, size);
 
 	if (exts_len != parsed_ext_len)
 		add_failure(edid, "The data size does not match the encoded block count.");
